+class TheWallIsSeenByTheTreeNotTheCommand(_Engine):
+    """LD-47 (2026-09-16): the wall-write row judges the command text, so it
+    refused `git checkout -- ops/devlane/task/jobs.json` under an ordinary
+    grant and did not refuse the python script that had rewritten the same
+    file with Path.write_text a minute earlier under that same grant. The
+    wall-state row reads the tree after the call instead, so the writing
+    interpreter does not matter.
+
+    Planted faults it catches: a wall file rewritten by a script whose
+    target the command text never spells; the same under an open grant of
+    class other (LD-47's own case); a new file under a wall directory; the
+    Write tool on a wall path. Clean neighbours it passes: a clean tree, a
+    non-wall file changed, and the wall changed with an open wall grant,
+    which is the authority the row asks for.
+    """
